  "notes": "West leads the ♠Q against 3NT which South wins. There are only 4 top tricks (2 spades, and 2 diamonds). South can establish 4 club tricks once the ♣A is dislodged. The ♥K and ♥Q will also combine for a trick once the ♥A has been knocked out. By that time, however, the defense will have had time to establish and run their spades.\n\nThe diamond suit also offers the possibility of extra tricks. After South unblocks the ♦A and ♦K, he might try leading a heart towards the dummy. If West has the ♥A, the ♥Q will be a certain dummy entry. South will be able to take 6 diamond tricks and make at least 9 tricks.\n\nSouth can actually ensure the contract no matter where the ♥A is placed. After unblocking in diamonds, South should lead the ♥K. If the defense wins the ♥A, the ♥Q will provide an entry to dummy's diamonds.\n\nIf South is allowed to hold the ♥K, he can knock out the ♣A and again take 9 tricks (2 spades, the ♥K, 2 diamonds, and 4 clubs).",
